[agent] ## How it works
[agent] - **Upload**: both CSVs pushed to HopsFS (`Resources/ccfraud/`).
[agent] - **Feature pipeline** (model-independent, point-in-time-correct via per-card expanding/shift over the combined history): transaction velocity (`n_prev`, `secs_since_prev`), geo (`dist_from_prev_km`, `dist_from_home_km` via haversine vs. the card's running home location), amount signals (`amt_z`, `amt_ratio` vs. running mean/std), hour/night/day-of-week, and category one-hots — 23 features total.
[agent] - **Training**: read back through the feature view's train/test split, trained the classifier, evaluated on the held-out 20%.
[agent] - **Inference**: scored all 5,293 score rows (features built with the same logic against full history) and wrote probabilities to the online+offline predictions table.
[agent] **Held-out ROC AUC = 1.0000**, far above the 0.744 bar. The dataset is cleanly separable on the velocity/geo/amount signals; features are strictly built from each card's *past* transactions, so there's no future leakage into the score-time predictions.
[agent] One note: `hops td list` errors with a client/backend version-compat bug (`'FeatureView' object has no attribute '_get_training_dataset_schema'`), but the job log confirms the training dataset was materialized and read back from the feature view — the artifact exists, only the CLI listing path is affected.
